    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that... but sitting with it just feels like drowning. i was thinking about this concept for a new piece, though. about how nothing is truly beautiful unless it's fleeting, and how there's this weird, dark kind of perfection in the moment something finally breaks or ends. like, maybe the only way to actually make something \"real\" is to let everything go completely. does that even make sense?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
